userStories.description:
**Goal** — Add a safe main-checkout preparation primitive that admits only clean, same-repository PR branches with ledger-only local commits.

**Motivation** — `nax bot fix` pushes from `.nax-wt/bot-pr-<n>-<suffix>`, built from the PR head, so the local commit is never pushed.

**Approach** — 5. **In-place checkout and review (#2660).**
- `--in-place` (on `withBotOptions`, so on both `review` and `fix`) sets `inPlace: true` on `BotReviewInput` and `BotFixInput`. `withBotInput` adds the key only when the flag is set (conditional spread), so inputs without the flag are unchanged.
- A new module, `src/bot/checkout-in-place.ts`, exports `prepareInPlaceCheckout`. It uses `_checkoutDeps` (`runGit`, `ensureGitExcludes`, `snapshotBaseNax`, `mkdtemp`, `rm`) and `cleanupCheckout`, the new export of `checkout.ts`'s `cleanup`.
- It returns a `PrCheckout` with:
  - `worktree` = the repo root;
  - `inPlace` = `true`;
  - `startHead` = the local HEAD sha read at prepare time;
  - `baseSha` and `mergeBase` from `fetchCheckoutRefs`;
  - `hasBaseNax` and `snapshotDir` from `snapshotBaseNax`;
  - `changedFiles` = the paths changed from `mergeBase` to `info.headSha` (`diff --name-only -z --no-renames <mergeBase> <info.headSha>`). A local ledger commit is therefore never part of the PR's change list.
- It first runs `ensureGitExcludes(repoRoot)`, so the bot's own run artifacts under `.nax/features/*/workflow/` are ignored.
- It then refuses, with `BOT_IN_PLACE_REFUSED`, in this order:
  - a cross-repository head;
  - a current branch other than `info.headRef`, or a detached HEAD;
  - a non-empty `git status --porcelain`, untracked files included, because `autoCommitIfDirty` would commit them;
  - a local HEAD that does not contain `info.headSha`;
  - local commits past `info.headSha` that change any path other than a `decisions.jsonl` directly under one feature directory.
  The feature directory is matched with `PROJECT_FEATURES_DIR` and `featureDir`, never an open-coded `.nax/features` string.
- It fetches through `fetchCheckoutRefs` (renamed export of `fetchRefs`), and never runs `worktree add` or `pinInstructions`. Skipping the pin is safe because in-place runs only on a trusted, same-repository PR. `dispose` deletes only the two checkout refs and the snapshot directory.
- `runBotReview` with `inPlace` refuses an untrusted PR (`--in-place needs a trusted PR`). After its pre-run steps it re-checks `git status --porcelain`. When dirty, it returns `refused` with reason `in-place checkout not clean after setup`.

**Scope** — In: preparation module, PrCheckout fields, shared checkout helper exports and cleanup, bot barrel export, stubbed git and real-repo safety tests. Out: the CLI and runBotReview wiring described above is US-006; runBotFix wiring, gate/saved-fix behavior and pre-push branch validation are US-007; ledger carry and graph transport are US-008/009. `--in-place` never runs for a cross-repository head or an untrusted PR, and never fetches into or switches the user's branch. In-place mode never resets, rebases or reattaches the user's checkout: fix commits a failed in-place run leaves on the local branch stay there.

**Interface** — `src/bot/checkout-in-place.ts`: `prepareInPlaceCheckout(input: { repoRoot; ref; info; suffix }): Promise<PrCheckout>`. Use the existing PrRef/PrInfo types for ref/info and string paths/suffix. `PrCheckout` (`src/bot/checkout.ts`). Target: adds `readonly inPlace?: boolean` and `readonly startHead?: string`. `fetchRefs` and `cleanup` (`src/bot/checkout.ts`, module-private). Target: exported as `fetchCheckoutRefs` and `cleanupCheckout` with unchanged inputs and results; `preparePrCheckout` calls them unchanged. Export the new module from `src/bot/index.ts`.

Failure handling: An in-place precondition fails — `BOT_IN_PLACE_REFUSED` naming the precondition; the CLI prints it and exits 1; nothing is fetched for the first three preconditions (CLI wiring is US-006). The fetched head differs from `info.headSha` in in-place mode — `BOT_PR_HEAD_MOVED`; both checkout refs deleted. A git command in the local-commit check fails in in-place mode — `BOT_CHECKOUT_FAILED`; both checkout refs deleted. The specifically defined `merge-base --is-ancestor <headSha> HEAD` exit 1 is a normal negative ancestry result, not an unexpected git failure: it keeps `BOT_IN_PLACE_REFUSED` with `pull first` and deletes both refs. Cleanup must omit any worktree argument that could remove the main checkout, including on failure.

**Goal** — Add the shared CLI flag and route trusted in-place reviews through the new checkout with a post-setup clean check.

**Motivation** — On #2659 and #2649 it was pushed by hand afterwards, which re-ran full CI each time.

